<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Salima Machamba</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1874">1874</a>–<a href="/years/1964">1964</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Salima Machamba was the last queen of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moheli">Mohéli</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/comoro-islands">Comoros</a>, a descendant of the Merina royal family of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a>. She came to the throne as a child under a French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> and in 1901 married a French gendarme, moving to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. She abdicated, and in 1909 Mohéli was annexed by France and attached to the colony of Mayotte and Dependencies.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/salima-machamba.jpg" alt="Salima Machamba" width="320" height="409" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:La_Reine_Salima.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
